integ5: tests: the FP8 KV glue test's fake module records up to 128 kernels and 32 shared-memory opt-ins.

cuda_kv8_test's "the glue resolves the paged symbols and opts their chunks into the window's shared memory" keeps every
cuFuncSetAttribute call of glue.Kernels.load in a 16-entry array. 3f94715d makes 10 opt-ins; attn5 0068 adds 6
(tf_glm_chunks_*_fused: 16, still fits) and glue5 0070 adds 1 (tf_glm_chunks_16_fp8_paged_segs: 11). Together they make
17, so the test panicked (index out of bounds) in the integrated stack only (test-glm-fp8-kv-host and test-cuda-host).
Test-only: no engine code changes.

